children.description:
The main expected results are: 
- 15 SMEs assessed and reports on RECP improvements developed; 
- 10 business plans to implement RECP measures prepared, 
- 15 experts trained on RECP methodology; 
- 2 RECP Clubs established and 12 modules implemented for about 20 enterprises in two selected regions (Gagauzia and Kahul); 
- RECP action plans developed by about 20 enterprises; 
- feasibility study of Eco-Industrial Parks framework application at Tracom IP and Valkanes FEZ is completed, 
-2 reports with recommendations are developed; 
- 2 specialized RECP training modules implemented.

projects.description:
Business support infrastructure in targeted regions for innovative SMEs development and trade promotion strengthened;
Cooperation between businesses and business associations, including across post-conflict divides, promoted.
Expert-oriented businesses assisted to extend their activities, business support organization capacitated for advocating and services provision for their members.

"The draft of the national immunization programme  development is initiated and submitted to MoH, 
COVID-19: 
National Deployment Vaccination Plan is developed and implemented;
SimEx of the vaccine deployment conducted; vaccination coordination and planning; 
Action plans are done according to evidence based information from SAGE and NITAG recommendations;
Enhanced and strengthening of coordination bodies (Coordination team, NITAG, ICC) with approved internal regulations and SOPs;
NRA capacity is strengthening in accelerating process of COVID-19 vaccines approval in the country;
Development of the immunization information system implemented in Primary Health Care system (SIAAMP) of the routine immunization;
Development and implementation of RVC19 (electronic information system for COVID-19 vaccination);
Supportive supervision visits to PHC:
Two communication immunization campaign for increasing demand on routine immunization and COVID-19
Capacity building of HCW (1387 vaccination centers)."

"Effective facilitation of confidence-building space for stakeholders to identify, recommend and test steps towards a joint model of cooperation on Gender Based Violence (GBV);
Advocacy and communication to support raising the GBV awareness and links to the settlement process with the 5+2 and other relevant actors;
Change in behaviour of practitioners (e.g. police, social and health sector) through trainings, specific study visit, expertise sharing, and development and piloting of practical tools that supports the effective running of shelter;
Running of shelter effectively and plan for transferring ownership of shelter to de facto authorities delivered."

"1) Completing the development of the informational system on Demographic and Social Statistics;
2) Review additional administrative data sources to be integrated into the informational system. 
3) Study visit to EU and India on use of administrative data in statistial work. "

